### Azure AI Search — ACL-trimmed queries against the SharePoint index
# Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
#
# Tokens (PowerShell, azd login as the admin):
#   $env:SEARCH_ADMIN_TOKEN = (azd auth token --scope https://search.azure.com/.default -o json | ConvertFrom-Json).token
# A persona's user token: sign in to the web app as the persona, open the browser dev tools,
# and copy the Authorization header of any /api/search request.
#
# Copy values from `azd env get-values` into a .env file next to this file (gitignored):
#   SEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://<service>.search.windows.net
#   SEARCH_ADMIN_TOKEN=...
#   PERSONA_TOKEN=...

@endpoint = {{$dotenv SEARCH_ENDPOINT}}
@index = sharepoint-acl-index
@api = 2026-08-01-preview
@adminToken = {{$dotenv SEARCH_ADMIN_TOKEN}}
@personaToken = {{$dotenv PERSONA_TOKEN}}

### 1. No user token -> ACL-protected chunks are NOT returned (count should be 0)
POST {{endpoint}}/indexes/{{index}}/docs/search?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "search": "AURORA", "count": true, "select": "title,path" }

### 2. Same query as a persona -> trimmed to what that persona can read
POST {{endpoint}}/indexes/{{index}}/docs/search?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
x-ms-query-source-authorization: {{personaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "search": "AURORA", "count": true, "select": "title,path" }

### 3. Elevated read (Search Index Data Contributor) -> everything, with the stored ACLs
#    Note: x-ms-enable-elevated-read can't be combined with x-ms-query-source-authorization.
POST {{endpoint}}/indexes/{{index}}/docs/search?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
x-ms-enable-elevated-read: true
Content-Type: application/json

{ "search": "*", "count": true, "top": 50, "select": "title,path,site,UserIds,GroupIds" }

### 4. Hybrid + semantic query as a persona (what the Ask tab retrieves)
POST {{endpoint}}/indexes/{{index}}/docs/search?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
x-ms-query-source-authorization: {{personaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "search": "superconducting qubits",
  "count": true,
  "top": 5,
  "select": "title,path",
  "queryType": "semantic",
  "semanticConfiguration": "semantic-config",
  "vectorQueries": [{ "kind": "text", "text": "superconducting qubits", "fields": "chunk_vector", "k": 50 }]
}

### 5. Codeword per folder (run as each persona)
#   BLUEBIRD  Research/Public    -> Alice, Bob, Carol
#   AURORA    Research/Quantum   -> Alice
#   KESTREL   Research/Bio       -> Carol
#   NIGHTJAR  Finance/Reports    -> Bob
#   OSPREY    HR/Confidential    -> nobody (site not granted to the ingestion app)
POST {{endpoint}}/indexes/{{index}}/docs/search?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
x-ms-query-source-authorization: {{personaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "search": "BLUEBIRD AURORA KESTREL NIGHTJAR OSPREY", "searchMode": "any", "count": true, "select": "title,path" }

### 6. Indexer status (one per site)
GET {{endpoint}}/indexers('ixr-hr')/search.status?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 7. Refresh ACLs after a parent-scope (site/library/folder) permission change
POST {{endpoint}}/indexers('ixr-research')/search.resync?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "options": ["permissions"] }

### 8. Then run the indexer
POST {{endpoint}}/indexers('ixr-research')/search.run?api-version={{api}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
